<section style="padding:96px 24px 40px;"><div style="max-width:860px;margin:0 auto;"><div class="rich"><p>Hub City Tank Co handles buried oil tank removal across New Brunswick, from Moncton and Dieppe out to Shediac, Sackville and everywhere in between. Underground oil tanks were common on properties heated before the 1980s, and most homeowners only find out about them when a home inspector, insurance company or lender starts asking questions. If that's where you are right now, take a breath. This is a solvable problem, and we deal with it every week.</p><p>Our crew locates the tank, excavates it safely, pumps out any leftover oil, and tests the soil underneath before we backfill. If the ground is clean, you'll have documentation proving it. If it's not, we walk you through the cleanup step by step, including the required notification to the provincial environment department. Either way, you get a <strong>free written estimate</strong> before we put a shovel in the ground. Call <strong>(506) 802-3471</strong> to get started.</p></div></div></section>
